<newsitem itemid="619687" id="root" date="1997-05-28" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Crookes Bros yr headline EPS rises.</title>
<headline>Crookes Bros yr headline EPS rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		128.8	 vs     98.1</p>
<p>    - attrib		  129.9	 vs    211.6</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  46.0	 vs     36.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	    15.59	vs     25.39</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    22.58	vs     30.70</p>
<p>    Tax			   6.99	vs	5.31</p>
<p>    Net interest received   3.46	vs	0.70</p>
<p>    Revenue		    82.49	vs     69.22</p>
<p>    Abnormal items	    0.13	vs     13.62</p>
<p>Div payable July 15, 1997</p>
<p>on register June 20, 1997</p>
<p>Full name: Crookes Brothers Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Crookes Bros said should favourable growing conditions throughout the country prevail, the group's operations should continue to look forward to improved results.</p>
<p>It said improved results were due to significant contributions from sugar cane which was partially offset by a reduction in grain earnings because of adverse weather conditions.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
